# PowerPoint files stay out of git.
#
# This repo is deliberately all-text — HTML, CSS, JS, markdown — so everything in
# it diffs. A .pptx is a zip of XML: git can't diff it, and every regeneration
# adds a fresh ~1 MB blob to history permanently.
#
# What this currently keeps out:
#   docs/Demo PPT Template - Octave.pptx        the brand template (belongs in
#                                               Octave's own store, not here)
#   docs/archive/EAM-Dev-Leadership-Deck-2026-08-25.pptx  a meeting artifact,
#                                               generated from the review doc
#                                               beside it in docs/archive/
#   docs/EAM-Mobile-Project-Scope.pptx          the vision/scope deck, rebuilt
#                                               by docs/scripts/build-scope-deck.js
#
# Each deck is reproducible from something that IS tracked — the review doc for
# the archived one, and `docs/scripts/build-scope-deck.js` for the scope deck
# (its content comes from docs/Total Project Scope Summary brief.md, its brand
# chrome from the template above). So the source of truth is in git even though
# the binaries are not. That is the whole bargain: if you add a .pptx here,
# add the thing that regenerates it too, or this rule stops being true.
# If a .pptx ever needs committing on purpose, use `git add -f`.
*.pptx
*.potx
*.ppt

# node_modules should never appear here (no build step by design), but a stray
# `npm install` while generating a deck would otherwise leave one behind.
node_modules/
